<!-- Earnings Statement, payroll-register layout: an indented identity block over a wide
     ledger of earnings and statutory withholding, with employee-paid benefits carried in
     the Other Benefits and Information panel on the right.

     Column mechanics worth knowing before editing:
       - Both ledgers run on a SIX-column grid with a narrow empty spacer column before
         Year To Date. That spacer is what produces the two separate underscores in the
         reference rather than one continuous rule; give every row its spacer cell.
       - Header rules are borderBottom on the individual heading cells, so a rule spans
         exactly the columns whose cells carry one. No colspan anywhere.
       - Optional lines (overtime, bonus, state paid leave, each benefit) are their own
         renderIf tables repeating the same fixed widths, since renderIf drops a table but
         cannot drop a row.

     Sized for the printable page: 720 x 960 CSS px. See CLAUDE.md, one stub one sheet. -->
